#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Nodes.rst:161
msgid "FAQs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Nodes.rst:163
msgid "What is the difference between a node and an executable?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Nodes.rst:164
msgid ""
"A node is a participant on the ROS graph. An executable is the program you "
"run, for example with ``ros2 run``, which starts a process. One process can "
"contain one or more nodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Nodes.rst:168
msgid "How do nodes find each other?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Nodes.rst:169
msgid ""
"Through discovery. When a node starts, the middleware advertises its "
"presence to other nodes on the same ROS domain. Their publishers, "
"subscriptions, and other endpoints can then connect automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Nodes.rst:173
msgid "Do all nodes in a system need to use the same programming language?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Nodes.rst:174
msgid ""
"No. Client libraries provide a common way to communicate, so a C++ node can "
"talk to a Python node over the same interfaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Nodes.rst:177
msgid "Why might two nodes fail to connect?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Nodes.rst:178
msgid "Common causes are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Nodes.rst:180
msgid "The nodes use different ROS domain IDs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Nodes.rst:181
msgid ""
"Discovery is limited, for example, ``ROS_AUTOMATIC_DISCOVERY_RANGE`` is set "
"to ``LOCALHOST`` and the nodes are on different machines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Nodes.rst:182
msgid "The nodes use different, incompatible middleware (RMW) implementations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Nodes.rst:183
msgid "The topic, service, or action names or types do not match."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Nodes.rst:184
msgid "The QoS settings of a publisher and a subscription are incompatible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Nodes.rst:185
msgid "A firewall or network configuration blocks discovery or data traffic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Nodes.rst:187
msgid "What is the difference between composable nodes and lifecycle nodes?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Nodes.rst:188
msgid ""
"Composable nodes are components that can run together in a single process. "
"Lifecycle nodes move through defined states so resources are started and "
"shut down in a controlled order."
msgstr ""
